    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Workflow 3 — Lead Qualifier  *(optional)*\n\nReads each lead's website and writes a **Fit** verdict to Airtable. It decides **who** you email — it never writes a word of **what** you email.\n\n**Why not AI-personalized copy?** A generated opener (\"I came across your portfolio of transitional kitchen remodels...\") is the most recognizable pattern in cold email — it reads as *more* of a pitch, not less. And anything a model writes into a live send is untestable. Targeting is where the leverage is at 30 sends/day: not emailing a roofer beats any phrasing.\n\n**Fail-open, everywhere.** A dead site, a timeout, an API outage → `Unsure`, which is still contacted. Only an explicit `No` is skipped. Never running this workflow at all leaves Workflow 1 behaving exactly as before.",
        "height": 400,
        "width": 1300,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "Note 6",
      "name": "Note 6",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -460,
        -480
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### Where the URL comes from\n1. a `Website` column, if you have one\n2. otherwise the email domain — `dana@mapleridgekitchens.com` → `mapleridgekitchens.com`\n\nFree mailboxes (gmail, yahoo, …) tell us nothing, so those leads are recorded as `Unsure` and contacted normally.",
        "height": 240,
        "width": 420,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "Note 7",
      "name": "Note 7",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1080,
        180
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### Cost\n`claude-sonnet-5` at low effort, ~1.5k input tokens per page:\n\n**≈ $4 per 1,000 leads.**\n\nCheaper than the verification credits saved on leads that were never a fit.",
        "height": 200,
        "width": 420,
        "color": 3
      },
      "id": "Note 8",
      "name": "Note 8",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        2620,
        400
      ]
    }
